  "body": "We have a number of examples of JavaScript code in the spec; e.g.:\r\n\r\nhttps://c.whatwg.org/multipage/introduction.html#a-quick-introduction-to-html:attr-hyperlink-href-3\r\n\r\nAs with other examples, those are all marked up with `pre` elements — but unlike the WebIDL examples which have `class=idl`, and the CSS examples, which have `class=css`, those JavaScript code examples have no `class` attribute. So we should add `class=js` to all of them.\r\n\r\nAmong other reasons, putting `class=js` on the would enable them be syntax-highlighted correctly. ",
